uns, NOT coerced to the \"\" null sentinel.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","T5b"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.275,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'resolve each with the existing resolvers' and resolvers 'time out at 30 s' (Measurement)","Test (b) covers 'resolvers return None' but not resolver timeout/raise","'The persisted authorship ledger is identical to the pre-change ledger' could be violated if a timeout is recorded as \"\" (null) while the in-lock fallback would have eventually resolved it"],"finding":"The plan specifies pre-resolution behavior when resolvers return None (-> \"\" -> null commit) but does not specify behavior when a resolver TIMES OUT during pre-resolution (the 30s resolver timeout is in-scope for being called, even though changing it is out of scope).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f497985336115861a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 and Testing case (b)","norm_id":"n363e4f25cea533e5","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A position's resolver walk exceeds 30s during pre-resolution on a loaded host"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 1, distinguish resolver outcomes: None -> \"\" (durably unresolvable); timeout/exception -> leave the position ABSENT from the returned map copy so the existing in-lock fallback handles it, preserving ledger equality.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_ju